---
import CommunityLayout from '../components/CommunityLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, FEEDBACK_EMAIL } from '../lib/contact';
---

<CommunityLayout
  title="Privacy policy | iDuckConvert"
  description="What iDuckConvert does and does not do with your files and your data. Files are processed in your browser and are not uploaded."
  before="Privacy"
  mark="policy"
  intro="Short version: your files stay on your device. Here is the longer version, in plain words."
>
  <section class="card p-5" aria-labelledby="files">
    <h2 id="files" class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight">Your files</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
      Every iDuckConvert tool opens, changes and saves your files inside your own browser. Your files are not uploaded to our
      servers, and we cannot see them or keep a copy. The one thing fetched from elsewhere is the ffmpeg engine for audio and video, a public code file that is downloaded from the jsDelivr CDN the first time you convert media; your file is not part of that request. When you close the tab they are gone from the page.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card p-5" aria-labelledby="collect">
    <h2 id="collect" class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight">What we collect</h2>
    <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-6 leading-relaxed">
      <li>
        <strong>Ordinary web requests.</strong> Our host, Cloudflare, receives the technical details any website receives when a
        page is loaded (such as your IP address, the page asked for and your browser type) and may keep them in standard
        server logs for security and reliability.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your theme choice.</strong> If you pick light or dark mode, it is saved in your browser local storage so the
        site remembers it. It never leaves your device. You can clear it on the <a class="link" href="/settings/">Settings</a>
        page.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Messages you choose to send.</strong> The feedback and request forms open an email in your own mail app. We only
        receive what you send, at the address you see on those pages ({FEEDBACK_EMAIL}). For anything else, write to {CONTACT_EMAIL}.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">We do not have accounts, so we hold no sign-up data. We do not sell personal data.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="card p-5" aria-labelledby="ads">
    <h2 id="ads" class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight">Ads and measuring visits</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
      iDuckConvert may show advertising in the future to cover its costs, and may use a privacy-focused visit counter. If that
      happens, ad and measurement providers may set cookies or collect data about your visit, and where the law requires it we
      will ask for your consent first and update this page before turning them on. Ads are never placed over the area where you
      add or download files, and they never receive your files.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card p-5" aria-labelledby="ai">
    <h2 id="ai" class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight">AI tools</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
      iDuckConvert has no AI tools. If that ever changes, the page will say clearly where your data goes, and this page will list which tools.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card p-5" aria-labelledby="rights">
    <h2 id="rights" class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight">Your choices and contact</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
      You can ask what we hold about you, or ask us to delete it, using the <a class="link" href="/feedback/">feedback form</a>.
      Because we keep so little, there is usually nothing beyond server logs. This policy may change; the date below shows when
      it last did.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">Last updated: 13 November 2026. Operated by Basic App Company.</p>
  </section>
</CommunityLayout>
